### Logic Implementation

| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Recommendation |
| --- | ---------- | ------- | ---------- | ---------------- |
| 1 | 🔴 CRITICAL | `update_env_file()` wraps values in double quotes (`f'{key}="{value}"'`), but `parse_env_file()` strips both `"` and `'` via `.strip('"').strip("'")`. If a value contains an embedded double quote (e.g. an API key with `"`), the round-trip corrupts the value. No escaping is performed. | `tools/lib/envfile.py` `update_env_file()` L~45, `parse_env_file()` L~20 | Implement proper escaping: escape `"` as `\"` before writing, and unescape on read. Alternatively, use a single consistent quoting strategy and document it. Add round-trip test: `write → read → compare`. |
| 2 | 🔴 CRITICAL | `retry_api()` in `gdrive.py` retries on ALL exceptions including non-transient errors (403 Permission Denied, 404 Not Found, invalid credentials). This causes 4 retries × backoff delay for errors that will never succeed, wasting ~20 seconds and masking the real error. | `tools/backup/gdrive.py` `retry_api()` L~55 | Catch only transient exceptions (`ConnectionError`, `TimeoutError`, `HttpError` with status 429/500/502/503). Let 401/403/404 propagate immediately. Add `from googleapiclient.errors import HttpError` and check `e.resp.status`. |
| 3 | 🟡 WARNING | `remove_mcp_servers()` in `connect.py` wraps `engine()` call in `try/except RuntimeError` and returns empty list on failure. This silently hides configuration errors — the user sees "no servers removed" when the real issue is a parse failure. | `tools/connect/connect.py` `remove_mcp_servers()` | Re-raise or log the error via `log_err()` before returning empty list. At minimum, distinguish "no matching servers found" from "failed to parse config file". |
| 4 | 🟡 WARNING | `cmd_run()` in `arwaky.py` for internal tools checks specific tool IDs (`lint`, `vision`, `qwen-web`, `blender`) with hardcoded `if tool.id in {...}` blocks. Adding a new internal tool requires modifying this function. The `mnemosyne` and `workspace` vendor tools are not handled. | `tools/cli/arwaky.py` `cmd_run()` L~220-240 | Refactor to a dispatch table or add `runner` field to `manifest.json` per tool (e.g. `"runner": "cargo"` or `"runner": "uv"`). Eliminate hardcoded tool ID checks. |
| 5 | 🟡 WARNING | `list_all_files()` in `gdrive.py` bounds pagination at 50 pages but only prints a warning to stderr. The caller receives a truncated list with no indication that results are incomplete, potentially missing backup files during restore. | `tools/backup/gdrive.py` `list_all_files()` | Return a tuple `(files, is_complete)` or raise an exception when pagination bound is hit. Callers must handle the incomplete case explicitly. |
| 6 | 🟢 INFO | `find_tool()` in `manifest.py` performs linear scan on every call. For CLI dispatch this is fine, but `load_tools()` re-reads and re-parses `manifest.json` on every invocation with no caching. | `tools/lib/manifest.py` `load_tools()` | Add module-level cache with `functools.lru_cache` or a simple `_cache` dict keyed on file mtime. Low priority since CLI is short-lived. |

